    <values>
        <field>Body__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">In the United States, this is where Memorial Day comes from. In 1868 a Union veterans' group set May 30 as Decoration Day, for decorating the graves of soldiers killed in the Civil War. Three years earlier, in Charleston, South Carolina, people who had just been freed decorated the graves of Union soldiers. That mourning is one root of the American holiday, now held on the last Monday in May.</value>
